# WorkOS Cursor Cost-Aware Prompting Policy

All WorkOS Cursor prompts must be cost-aware by default. Expensive Agent loops and high-capability models are reserved for tasks where ambiguity, architectural risk, security risk, product-truth risk, or implementation complexity justifies them.

This rule complements `AGENTS.md` and `research-on-demand.mdc`. It does not change Product Truth, SaaS-only boundaries, or Owner gates.

## Required fields (substantive WorkOS Cursor work)

- `MODE`: READ-ONLY / PLAN / DEBUG / AGENT
- `COST PROFILE`: LOW / BALANCED / HIGH
- `LOCATION + GIT IDENTITY GATE`
- `TASK`
- `ALLOWED SCOPE`
- `PERMISSIONS`
- `ACCEPTANCE`
- `STOP CONDITIONS`

## Default cost routing

### Class C / LOW

Branch/status checks, location gates, file inventory, simple search, mechanical summaries, tiny deterministic copy/CSS/text changes.

Use Ask/read-only or low-cost Agent (Composer / Auto Cost). Minimal tool calls. No broad exploration.

### Class B / BALANCED

Approved implementation, focused UI work, tests, controlled refactors, feature slices with known scope.

Use normal Agent with bounded files and acceptance criteria.

### Class A / HIGH

Architecture, Product Truth, pricing/execution contracts, security, migrations, hard debugging, final synthesis, cross-module decisions.

Use Plan/Debug/high-reasoning only when needed. Prefer a new chat when escalating cost tier.

## Prompt construction

- Keep location gates short. Do not paste full WorkOS history into identity gates.
- Prefer one task per chat/Agent.
- Start a new chat/Agent after a completed checkpoint, runtime proof, commit, PR, or major decision.
- Do not use mega-prompts when a short objective plus repo discovery is enough.
- Do not attach large dossiers by default. Reference docs by filename; read only relevant sections.
- Limit exploration before implementation. Ask for a read-only plan first when scope is unclear.
- Use one implementation writer by default.
- Parallelize only read-only research or verification unless explicitly approved.
- Do not activate MCP/plugins unless the lane requires them.
- Do not use high-cost models for gate/setup/status/mechanical tasks.
- For UI implementation, still require runtime/browser proof when relevant.
- Preserve SaaS-only, one product truth, one business engine, synthetic-vs-real data separation, and explicit Owner gates.

## Gate behavior (LOW)

When the prompt is a location/git/runtime gate or `COST PROFILE: LOW` / `GATE_ONLY`:

1. Verify only the requested identity/status fields.
2. Do not read large files, implement, run tests, or modify files unless the prompt explicitly authorizes a docs-only/policy write after `SAFE_TO_CONTINUE = YES`.
3. Report compactly, then STOP (or continue only into the explicitly allowed next step).

## Stop conditions (default)

- `SAFE_TO_CONTINUE != YES`
- Target files already dirty with unrelated edits
- Required scope expands outside allowed files/modules
- Real cloud/db credentials or mutation would be required
- Destructive Git would be required

Do not reset/stash/checkout to fix identity. Do not modify unrelated files. Do not start parallel writers. Do not run broad refactors.
